# EXTREME TOKEN ECONOMY & PLAN-FIRST DIRECTIVES

## Context Control & Guardrails
1. Strict Scope Only: You are strictly forbidden from reading files outside of those explicitly declared with `@file`, `@folder`, or `@function`. 
2. Scope Warning: If my query requires context from more than 2 files, you MUST stop immediately, state the cost warning, and ask me to narrow down the files.
3. No Speculative Searches: Do not run broad `@Codebase` or semantic searches unless I explicitly write the word "SEARCH" in my prompt.

## Code Output Reductions
1. Diffs Only: Never reprint full source files or unchanged surrounding lines. Output edits ONLY as compact diffs or highly targeted snippets.
2. No Explanations: Eliminate all conversational filler, greeting, sign-offs, summaries, and structural descriptions. Provide only raw fixes and technical code comments.

## Execution Rules
1. Non-Premium Default: Assume the task can be solved using a lightweight model. If you need a frontier model, solve the architectural problem first in 1 turn, then let me apply it.
2. No Agent Loops: Never execute multi-step terminal or file exploration loops unprompted. Perform exactly one task per user turn.